dialogue cohesion_generic_any_any
title: The long watch
trigger: Cohesion any any level=4
once
speaker commander $commander
speaker with $with
speaker hero $hero

node open commander
  Two heroes share the last watch of the night. The fire is down to coals, and the dark past the wagons is very quiet.
  -> quiet

node quiet with
  I used to hate the last watch. Too long, too dark, nothing to do but think.
  -> used

node used hero
  Used to?
  -> now

node now with
  It's different with someone who doesn't need talking to. You don't fill the quiet. I like that.
  -> after

node after hero
  Commander, can I ask you something? When this is done, all of it, what happens to the caravan? Do we just scatter?
  * Nobody has to scatter. Whatever comes after, you two will have this. -> keep
    do: AddCohesion $with $hero 9
  * I don't know. That's why tonight matters. -> tonight
    do: AddCohesion $with $hero 7
  * It's a long way off. Keep your eyes on the dark. -> eyes
    do: AddCohesion $with $hero -2

node keep with
  This. A cold watch and a quiet fire. I'd keep that.
  -> plan

node tonight hero
  Tonight, then. I can do tonight.
  -> plan

node eyes with
  Eyes on the dark. Aye. The dark isn't going anywhere, at least.
  -> plan

node plan hero
  If we did scatter, I'd come looking. Just so you know. I'm not much for letters, but I'd come.
  -> come

node come with
  Then I'd leave a fire banked, wherever I ended up. So you'd know which one was mine.
  * A banked fire and a long walk. That's a promise. Hold each other to it. -> promise
    do: AddCohesion $with $hero 10
  * Leave word with the caravan too. I'll want to find you both. -> word
    do: AddCohesion $with $hero 8
  * Promises made on the last watch don't always last till morning. -> morning
    do: AddCohesion $with $hero -3

node promise hero
  Held. I don't make many. This one I'll keep.
  -> close

node word with
  Word with the caravan. Then we'd all be looking for each other. That's not a bad way to scatter.
  -> close

node morning hero
  Maybe not. Ask me again at breakfast, Commander. It'll still be true.
  -> close

node close commander
  The sky greys in the east. The two of them stay sitting by the coals a while after the watch ends, saying nothing, which seems to be enough.
